                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east-central Texas, including the following\ncounties, Anderson, Freestone and Leon.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 AM CDT early this morning through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The soon to be remnants of Tropical Storm Edouard are expected to\nbring a localized swath of very heavy rain to portions of the\nFlood Watch. While most locations in the watch will see 1 to 3\ninches of rain, localized amounts of 4-6 inches will be possible\nthrough Thursday night.\n- weather.gov/safety/flood",
